1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,539
Why does no country own Antarctica?

2
00:00:02,889 --> 00:00:06,420
Antarctica is huge, about fourteen million square

3
00:00:06,420 --> 00:00:09,879
kilometers. That's bigger than the United States

4
00:00:09,879 --> 00:00:12,618
and Mexico combined, and almost all of

5
00:00:12,618 --> 00:00:14,131
it is covered in ice.

6
00:00:14,481 --> 00:00:17,909
Seven countries claim pieces of it: Argentina,

7
00:00:17,909 --> 00:00:21,559
Australia, Chile, France, New Zealand, Norway and

8
00:00:21,559 --> 00:00:24,539
the United Kingdom. Some of those claims

9
00:00:24,539 --> 00:00:27,073
even overlap, like slices of a pie

10
00:00:27,073 --> 00:00:29,159
fighting for the same space.

11
00:00:29,509 --> 00:00:32,143
But in 1959, during the Cold War,

12
00:00:32,143 --> 00:00:36,135
twelve countries signed the Antarctic Treaty. Even

13
00:00:36,135 --> 00:00:39,169
the United States and the Soviet Union

14
00:00:39,169 --> 00:00:39,727
agreed.

15
00:00:40,077 --> 00:00:42,798
The treaty froze every claim. No new

16
00:00:42,798 --> 00:00:46,122
claims, no military bases, no weapons tests,

17
00:00:46,122 --> 00:00:49,220
and no nuclear waste. The whole continent

18
00:00:49,220 --> 00:00:51,789
is reserved for peace and science.

19
00:00:52,139 --> 00:00:55,099
Today, fifty eight countries have joined the

20
00:00:55,099 --> 00:00:57,925
treaty. Scientists from all over the world

21
00:00:57,925 --> 00:01:01,019
live at research stations there, studying ice,

22
00:01:01,019 --> 00:01:02,230
climate and space.

23
00:01:02,580 --> 00:01:05,309
There's even a part of Antarctica that

24
00:01:05,309 --> 00:01:08,110
no country has ever claimed, Marie Byrd

25
00:01:08,110 --> 00:01:10,911
Land. It's one of the largest unclaimed

26
00:01:10,911 --> 00:01:11,988
areas on Earth.

27
00:01:12,338 --> 00:01:15,948
Antarctica is the coldest, windiest and driest

28
00:01:15,948 --> 00:01:19,872
continent. The lowest temperature ever measured by

29
00:01:19,872 --> 00:01:22,932
a weather station was minus eighty nine

30
00:01:22,932 --> 00:01:26,464
point two degrees Celsius, at Russia's Vostok

31
00:01:26,464 --> 00:01:27,719
Station in 1983.

32
00:01:28,069 --> 00:01:30,370
No one was born there and stays.

33
00:01:30,370 --> 00:01:33,677
Antarctica has no permanent population, just a

34
00:01:33,677 --> 00:01:36,841
few thousand scientists and staff in summer,

35
00:01:36,841 --> 00:01:39,141
and around a thousand in winter.

36
00:01:39,491 --> 00:01:42,461
Under all that ice are huge mineral

37
00:01:42,461 --> 00:01:45,940
and possibly oil reserves. But a protocol

38
00:01:45,940 --> 00:01:49,334
added in 1991 bans mining in Antarctica,

39
00:01:49,334 --> 00:01:50,777
at least for now.

40
00:01:51,127 --> 00:01:54,339
Tourism is growing, though. Every summer, tens

41
00:01:54,339 --> 00:01:57,062
of thousands of visitors arrive by ship

42
00:01:57,062 --> 00:02:00,065
to see penguins, whales and giant icebergs.

43
00:02:00,415 --> 00:02:02,168
Would you spend a winter at a

44
00:02:02,168 --> 00:02:04,707
research station in Antarctica? Tell me in

45
00:02:04,707 --> 00:02:05,493
the comments.

